        <strong>Everywhere else on this list</strong> (Velveteen Rabbit, Herbs & Rye, The Griffin, Here Kitty Kitty, Ghost Donkey, Ski Lodge, Pinky Ring, Cabinet of Curiosities/The Lock) — walk-in, no password or reservation needed. If a line forms, ask the door person/host directly — they can usually give you a wait estimate.
      </div></div>
      <div class="tip-box"><div class="tip-lbl">🚌 Big Bus Pairings</div><div class="tip-txt"><strong>Direct hits (at the stop):</strong> Here Kitty Kitty (Resorts World stop), The Underground (Mob Museum stop), Velveteen Rabbit (Arts District stop).<br><br><strong>Short walk from a stop:</strong> The Griffin & The Laundry Room (Mob Museum stop), 1923 Prohibition & Employees Only (TI stop), Cabinet of Curiosities/The Lock (High Roller stop), Ghost Donkey/Ski Lodge/Pinky Ring (MGM Grand stop — same as the Foodie Tour).<br><br><strong>Uber-only:</strong> Herbs & Rye is off-Strip on Sahara Ave, not near any Big Bus stop.</div></div>
      <div class="sec"><div class="sh"><div class="st">Speakeasy & Hidden Bars</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Employees Only Las Vegas ⭐</div><div class="rc-type">James Beard cocktails · Inside The Cosmopolitan · 🚌 TI stop · Top pick</div><div class="rc-desc">NYC speakeasy legend with a Vegas home inside The Cosmopolitan. Hidden entrance, extraordinary cocktails, late-night kitchen. Best after midnight — energy builds.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Bar/cocktail seating is walk-in only, first-come first-served — no reservations possible for that (this is their policy chain-wide). Ask the bartender for their current obsession. Tell them it's Larra's birthday. The bone marrow dishes are outstanding. If you need to reach the property directly for any reason, The Cosmopolitan's main line is <strong>(702) 698-7000</strong>.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: the Mata Hari (cognac, apricot, rose)</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.employeesonlylv.com" target="_blank">employeesonlylv.com ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('3708 Las Vegas Blvd S, Las Vegas, NV 89109',this)">📋 The Cosmopolitan · 3708 Las Vegas Blvd S</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">The Laundry Room</div><div class="rc-type">True speakeasy · 🚌 Mob Museum stop · Text (702) 701-1466 to reserve · Max 4 guests</div><div class="rc-desc">Through a literal laundromat (inside Commonwealth). Reservations by text only — required, not optional. Max 4 guests, 90-min slot. Fully bespoke cocktails — no menu.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Text <strong>(702) 701-1466</strong> to book ahead (fills up fast — try to text at least a few days out). Text that same number again when you arrive at Commonwealth to let them know you're there. Tell them it's a birthday. Dressy casual, no flip-flops/athletic wear, two-drink minimum + mandatory popcorn.</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.laundryroomlv.com" target="_blank">laundryroomlv.com ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('525 Fremont St, Las Vegas, NV 89101',this)">📋 525 Fremont St · Downtown</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Velveteen Rabbit</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 Arts District stop (same block!) · Where Vegas locals drink</div><div class="rc-desc">Seasonal menus, locally sourced, genuine craft. 10 minutes from the Strip, completely different world.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Small, cozy, and always changing — ask what's new on the seasonal list rather than ordering off an old menu photo.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: whatever's on the current seasonal cocktail list</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.thevelveteerabbitve.com" target="_blank">thevelveteerabbitve.com ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('1218 S Main St, Las Vegas, NV 89104',this)">📋 1218 S Main St · Arts District</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Herbs & Rye</div><div class="rc-type">🚫 Not near a Big Bus stop — Uber only · Late-night · 11 PM–2 AM happy hour</div><div class="rc-desc">Deeply committed to the craft. Encyclopedic classic cocktail knowledge. Best late-night option not on the Strip.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Go after 11 PM for the happy hour menu — same top-shelf cocktails, better price, and the room really comes alive.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: ask the bartender for an off-menu classic</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.herbsandrye.com" target="_blank">herbsandrye.com ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('3713 W Sahara Ave, Las Vegas, NV 89102',this)">📋 3713 W Sahara Ave</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">The Griffin</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 Mob Museum stop (short walk) · Fremont East · Gothic den</div><div class="rc-desc">Unmarked door on Fremont East opens into a dim, castle-like room split into cozy nooks — one side leans metal and dark, the other soft and lounge-y. A downtown institution for over a decade.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Grab one of the fireside couches if you can. Cash tends to move faster here than cards at the bar.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: their jukebox stocked with vinyl — pick something and own it</div><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('511 Fremont St, Las Vegas, NV 89101',this)">📋 511 Fremont St · Fremont East</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">The Underground at The Mob Museum</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 Mob Museum stop (literally there!) · Password changes weekly · Prohibition-era</div><div class="rc-desc">A genuine 1920s-style speakeasy hidden behind a bookcase in the basement of The Mob Museum, complete with a hidden distillery and a password whispered through a slot in the door.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 The password changes every week — check <strong>The Underground's Instagram (@theundergroundlv)</strong> the day of your visit for the current word. Find the side entrance around back (look for the wooden barrel near a green door), or if you have museum admission you can skip the password entirely and enter via the box office stairs inside. Go for the full distillery tour + tasting if time allows.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: a Prohibition-era classic like a Sidecar or Last Word</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://themobmuseum.org/exhibit/the-underground/" target="_blank">themobmuseum.org/underground ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('300 Stewart Ave, Las Vegas, NV 89101',this)">📋 300 Stewart Ave · Downtown</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Here Kitty Kitty Vice Den ⭐</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 Resorts World stop (literally there!) · Near Wynn AND steps from Sphere</div><div class="rc-desc">Tucked behind a bookcase inside Ms. Meow's Mamak Stall in the Famous Foods food hall. Asian-inspired decor, neon tigers on the wall, Prohibition-era cocktails with a Singaporean twist.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Tell the stall staff "here, kitty kitty" and they'll walk you through the hidden bookcase door. Resorts World is one of the two closest Big Bus stops to Sphere — this could be a perfect pre- or post-Wizard of Oz stop on Jul 10, and it's also an easy walk from Wynn any other night.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: ask for a bartender's choice — they'll surprise you</div><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('3000 S Las Vegas Blvd, Las Vegas, NV 89109',this)">📋 3000 S Las Vegas Blvd · Resorts World</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">1923 Prohibition Bar — Venetian</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 TI stop (short walk) · Walk-in, no password needed · Steps from Sphere & Wynn</div><div class="rc-desc">The original Mandalay Bay speakeasy's second, more exclusive location, right next door to Sphere and an easy walk from Wynn. New Orleans-style speakeasy with live music and burlesque on weekends.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 No password needed anymore and no reservation required for regular seating — just find the bookcase entrance and walk in. Fri/Sat has live burlesque + music 9:30-12:30 PM (no cover). Call <strong>(702) 586-8925</strong> if you want to reserve a table ahead or confirm what's happening that night.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: a bourbon-forward classic — this spot is bourbon-centric</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.1923lv.com/locations/" target="_blank">1923lv.com ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('The Venetian Resort, Grand Canal Shoppes, Las Vegas, NV 89109',this)">📋 Grand Canal Shoppes · The Venetian</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Ghost Donkey</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 MGM Grand stop (~15-20 min walk) · The Cosmopolitan · Mezcal & tequila</div><div class="rc-desc">Look for the door with the donkey on it on the 2nd floor food court. Small, loud, and packed with Christmas lights — a fun, unpretentious tequila party.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Can get crowded early — it's a favorite. Great truffle nachos if you want a bite with your drink. Same Big Bus stop as the Jul 10 Foodie Tour, if you want a nightcap after.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: their tequila flights</div><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('The Cosmopolitan, 3708 Las Vegas Blvd S, Las Vegas, NV 89109',this)">📋 The Cosmopolitan</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">The Ski Lodge</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 MGM Grand stop (~15-20 min walk) · The Cosmopolitan · Alpine dive bar</div><div class="rc-desc">Ski-chalet themed hidden bar inside The Cosmopolitan — cozy, kitschy, and capped at just 30 people, so it never feels overwhelming.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Small capacity means it can fill up fast on weekends — worth checking in early in the night. Same building as Ghost Donkey.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: their hot toddy or spiked cocoa</div><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('The Cosmopolitan, 3708 Las Vegas Blvd S, Las Vegas, NV 89109',this)">📋 The Cosmopolitan</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">The Pinky Ring by Bruno Mars</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 MGM Grand stop (~15-20 min walk) · Bellagio · Live band</div><div class="rc-desc">Bruno Mars' own cocktail lounge inside Bellagio — 1970s-inspired design, curated cocktail list, and his band The Hooligans occasionally play surprise sets.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Reserve ahead for a table; walk-ins are possible but seating fills fast, especially with live music.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: The Hooligan (tequila, Cointreau, agave, lime, jalapeño-Tajín rim)</div><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('Bellagio, 3600 Las Vegas Blvd S, Las Vegas, NV 89109',this)">📋 Bellagio</div></div>
        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Cabinet of Curiosities / The Lock</div><div class="rc-type">🚌 High Roller stop (~10 min walk) · Horseshoe · Two connected hidden bars</div><div class="rc-desc">Follow signs from the casino floor down to Cabinet of Curiosities — an eclectic, gorgeous room of oddities — which connects to The Lock, entered through a crawl-through vault door puzzle.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Do both in one stop — they're connected. The Lock's vault-door entrance is a fun photo moment. Horseshoe is walkable from the High Roller stop, so easy to fold into a Big Bus day.</div><div class="rc-ck">🥃 Must: ask for their seasonal specialty cocktail</div><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('Horseshoe Las Vegas, 3645 Las Vegas Blvd S, Las Vegas, NV 89109',this)">📋 Horseshoe Las Vegas</div></div>
