          <div class="exc-body">
            <div class="exc-desc">A scenic drive through Ketchikan brings you to the UTV Base Camp, nestled in a protected rainforest property. After a safety briefing and gear-up, you'll caravan out into the wild terrain for a 60-minute, adrenaline-fueled guided trek — over bridges and old logging roads, through the George Inlet Fjords, with views of the Mahoney Glacial Cirque. Next, climb aboard an enclosed 46-foot sightseeing vessel for a 7-mile coastal cruise to George Inlet Lodge, a converted 1940s cannery bunkhouse — keep watch for eagles along the way. At the lodge, settle in for a craft beer tasting (five beers from two local breweries) paired with crab chowder, smoked salmon dip, steaming hot Dungeness crab, and blueberry-topped cheesecake. Ketchikan is the "Salmon Capital of the World," sitting at the edge of the Tongass National Forest — the largest national forest in the US. Ship in port 7 AM–4 PM giving you a full day. Helmets provided; min age 8; must be 21+ for the beer tasting.</div>
            <div style="margin-top:10px"><div class="exc-full-toggle" onclick="event.stopPropagation();toggleExcFull(this)"><span>📄 Full Excursion Description</span><span class="exc-full-chev">▶</span></div><div class="exc-full-body"><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.65;padding:8px 2px 2px">This half-day adventure starts with a safety briefing and gear-up at the UTV Base Camp on a protected rainforest property outside Ketchikan. You'll drive your own off-road UTV in a guided caravan for about an hour, crossing bridges and old logging roads through the George Inlet Fjords, with views of the Mahoney Glacial Cirque along the way. From there, you'll board a 46-foot enclosed catamaran for a scenic 7-mile cruise along the coast to George Inlet Lodge, a converted former cannery bunkhouse — keep an eye out for eagles en route. At the lodge, you'll sit down to a craft beer tasting (several pours from local breweries) paired with a Dungeness crab feast that includes crab chowder, smoked salmon dip, steaming Dungeness crab, and a slice of blueberry cheesecake.</div><div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--tm);margin-top:6px;font-style:italic">Sourced from the tour operator's listing — Celebrity's own excursion page requires signing in to your reservation to view.</div></div></div>
            <div class="exc-links"><a class="exc-link" href="https://www.celebrity.com/cruise-excursions/alaska" target="_blank">Celebrity Excursions ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('Ketchikan, AK — meet at ship gangway 9:15 AM',this)">📋 Meet at gangway 9:15 AM</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:8px">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">👀 What to See</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.7">
            <strong>Creek Street</strong> — the boardwalk built over Ketchikan Creek, once the town's red-light district, now shops and galleries on pilings.<br>
            <strong>Totem poles</strong> — Saxman Native Village and Totem Bight State Historical Park both hold major collections of authentic Tlingit and Haida totems.<br>
            <strong>Misty Fjords National Monument</strong> — flightseeing tours over granite cliffs, waterfalls, and fjords if you have extra time.
