    <div class="panel" id="ak-port-skagway">
      <div class="sec"><div class="sh"><div class="st">🥾 Skagway, Alaska</div></div>
        <div id="daywx-ak-port-skagway"></div>
        <div class="tip-box"><div class="tip-lbl">Docked</div><div class="tip-txt">7:00 AM – 6:00 PM · Tuesday, Aug 18 · Your excursion: Small Group Ocean Raft Wildlife Adventure, 9:00 AM</div></div>
        <div class="exc-item" style="margin-bottom:10px">
          <div class="exc-hdr" onclick="toggleExc(this)">
            <div class="exc-bar" style="background:#0ea5e9"></div>
            <div class="exc-main"><div class="exc-day" style="color:#0284c7">🏔 Your Booked Excursion · 9:00 AM · ~3 hours</div><div class="exc-name">Small Group: Ocean Raft Wildlife Adventure 🦭🐋</div><div class="exc-meta">Order #195146374 · Guest: Larra · Max 12 guests</div></div>
            <div><div class="exc-price">$287.99</div><div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--ac);text-align:right;font-weight:700">10% LOYALTY</div></div>
            <div class="exc-chevron">▶</div>
          </div>
          <div class="exc-body">
            <div class="exc-desc">You'll suit up in a one-piece exposure suit (the same gear worn by US Coast Guard rescue teams), then board a 750-horsepower raft — the same style of boat used by the Coast Guard and Navy SEALs for search and rescue. With its deep-V hull surrounded by inflatable tubes, it's built to handle any sea condition while getting you close to shore. From there you'll race along the steep granite walls of Lynn Canal, North America's longest and deepest fjord, exploring hidden coves, waterfalls, and beaches. Your Coast Guard-certified captain makes multiple stops for photos and wildlife — eagles are nearly guaranteed, with frequent sightings of harbor seals, sea lions, otters, and (less commonly) whales — and occasionally cuts the engines so you can just take in the sound of the wilderness. Min age 10; max weight 350 lbs.</div>
            <div style="margin-top:10px"><div class="exc-full-toggle" onclick="event.stopPropagation();toggleExcFull(this)"><span>📄 Full Excursion Description</span><span class="exc-full-chev">▶</span></div><div class="exc-full-body"><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.65;padding:8px 2px 2px">You'll suit up in a full Mustang survival suit, goggles, and gloves before boarding a rigid inflatable boat (RIB) with an experienced local captain. The two-hour tour skirts close to shore along Lynn Canal — North America's longest and deepest fjord — stopping at hidden coves, waterfalls, and beaches for photos and wildlife spotting. Past trips have turned up whales, Steller sea lions, harbor seals, mountain goats, and plenty of bald eagles, with running narration from your captain throughout.</div><div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--tm);margin-top:6px;font-style:italic">Sourced from the tour operator's listing — Celebrity's own excursion page requires signing in to your reservation to view.</div></div></div>
            <div class="tip-box" style="margin-top:9px"><div class="tip-lbl">Wildlife Tips 🦅</div><div class="tip-txt">Bring binoculars! Sit toward the front for best visibility. Ocean Zodiacs get wet — bring a waterproof layer even if skies look clear. 9 AM = peak whale feeding time.</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:8px">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">👀 What to See</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.7">
            <strong>White Pass & Yukon Route Railway</strong> — a narrow-gauge train up through the same pass Gold Rush stampeders climbed in 1898, with dramatic mountain and gorge views.<br>
            <strong>Klondike Gold Rush National Historical Park</strong> — walk the preserved Gold Rush-era downtown and visitor center.<br>
            <a class="di-link" href="https://www.skagway.com" target="_blank">Skagway Official Site ↗</a> — port info, maps, and things to do
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:8px">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">🍽️ What to Try</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.7">Reindeer sausage from a downtown stand, and fresh-caught salmon at one of the harbor-side spots.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="border-left:4px solid #b8860b">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">🥃 The Speakeasy</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.7"><strong>Red Onion Saloon</strong> — a preserved 1898 brothel-turned-bar with a museum upstairs and a bawdy "Madam" walking tour. The most iconic bar in town — don't skip it.</div>
        </div>
