    <div class="panel" id="ak-port-victoria">
      <div class="sec"><div class="sh"><div class="st">🌺 Victoria, British Columbia</div></div>
        <div id="daywx-ak-port-victoria"></div>
        <div class="tip-box"><div class="tip-lbl">Last Stop</div><div class="tip-txt">Thursday, Aug 20 · Your excursion: Hop-On Hop-Off City Sightseeing, 6:30 PM</div></div>
        <div class="exc-item" style="margin-bottom:10px">
          <div class="exc-hdr" onclick="toggleExc(this)">
            <div class="exc-bar"></div>
            <div class="exc-main"><div class="exc-day">🏔 Your Booked Excursion · 6:30 PM · All-day pass</div><div class="exc-name">Hop-On Hop-Off City Sightseeing 🇨🇦</div><div class="exc-meta">Order #195146282 · Guest: Larra</div></div>
            <div><div class="exc-price">$52.99</div><div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--ac);text-align:right;font-weight:700">30% OFF</div></div>
            <div class="exc-chevron">▶</div>
          </div>
          <div class="exc-body">
            <div class="exc-desc">Victoria's Hop-On Hop-Off covers the Inner Harbour, Empress Hotel, Beacon Hill Park, and North America's oldest Chinatown. Ship docks at 5:30 PM and departs 11:59 PM — a beautiful evening in one of Canada's most charming cities. Golden hour light over the Inner Harbour with the illuminated Parliament buildings is extraordinary.</div>
            <div style="margin-top:10px"><div class="exc-full-toggle" onclick="event.stopPropagation();toggleExcFull(this)"><span>📄 Full Excursion Description</span><span class="exc-full-chev">▶</span></div><div class="exc-full-body"><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.65;padding:8px 2px 2px">An open-top double-decker bus loop with narrated commentary, departing from the Fairmont Empress Hotel on Government Street. The route covers 14 stops around Greater Victoria, including Chinatown/Fan Tan Alley, Bastion Square, Fisherman's Wharf, the Ogden Point cruise terminal and breakwater, Beacon Hill Park, Christ Church Cathedral, Craigdarroch Castle, and Oak Bay's village, marina, and beach hotel. Buses run roughly every hour, and your pass lets you hop off at any stop and catch a later bus to continue — a full loop without stopping takes about 90 minutes.</div><div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--tm);margin-top:6px;font-style:italic">Sourced from the tour operator's listing — Celebrity's own excursion page requires signing in to your reservation to view.</div></div></div>
            <div class="tip-box" style="margin-top:9px"><div class="tip-lbl">Victoria Evening Tips 🌅</div><div class="tip-txt">The Empress Hotel lobby bar has excellent cocktails — worth a stop. Float planes landing in the harbour at sunset are a sight. You have a late departure so enjoy Victoria fully — this is a gem of a city.</div></div>
            <div class="exc-links"><a class="exc-link" href="https://sightseeingvictoria.com/tours/hop-on-hop-off-citysights/" target="_blank">Victoria Hop-On Hop-Off ↗</a><div class="copy-b" onclick="copyAddr('Victoria, BC · Inner Harbour, Belleville St',this)">📋 Inner Harbour, Belleville St</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sh" style="margin-top:4px"><div class="st">🚌 Hop-On Hop-Off Route</div></div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:8px">
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.7">Loop starts and ends at the <strong>Fairmont Empress</strong> on the Inner Harbour, about 90 minutes for the full loop if you stay on, with buses every 30–45 min. Key stops to hop off at:</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.9;margin-top:8px">
            🏛️ <strong>Fairmont Empress</strong> (start/end) — iconic hotel, famous for afternoon tea<br>
            🏮 <strong>Chinatown / Fan Tan Alley</strong> — oldest Chinatown in Canada, great food and craft beer<br>
            🏰 <strong>Bastion Square</strong> — historic core, shops and cafés<br>
            🎣 <strong>Fisherman's Wharf</strong> — colorful floating houses, fish & chips from the floating stalls<br>
            🌳 <strong>Beacon Hill Park</strong> — totem poles, gardens, ocean views<br>
            🏚️ <strong>Craigdarroch Castle</strong> — Victorian-era mansion, worth the climb inside<br>
            ⛵ <strong>Oak Bay Village / Marina</strong> — quieter, upscale, good for a coffee break<br>
            🌊 <strong>Ogden Point Breakwater</strong> — walk the breakwater, whale-watching departures here too
          </div>
          <a class="di-link" href="https://www.tourismvictoria.com" target="_blank" style="display:inline-block;margin-top:8px">Tourism Victoria ↗</a> — Inner Harbour, Empress Hotel, evening options
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:8px">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">🍽️ What to Try</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.7">Nanaimo bars (BC's signature dessert), fresh Pacific salmon or fish & chips at Fisherman's Wharf, a pint at a Chinatown craft brewery, and afternoon tea at the Empress if you can swing it (book ahead — it's popular).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tip-box"><div class="tip-lbl">Worth Knowing</div><div class="tip-txt">Butchart Gardens isn't on the main hop-on-hop-off loop — it's a separate shuttle/combo ticket if you want to add it.</div></div>
        <div class="card hi" style="border-left:4px solid #b8860b">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">🥃 Speakeasy Picks</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.7">
            <strong>Artemis Whiskey Bar</strong> — a true hidden speakeasy; pick the correct book off a bookshelf to get the door to open, 200+ whiskeys on the menu. <a class="di-link" href="https://artemiswhiskey.ca/" target="_blank">Website ↗</a> <a class="di-link" href="https://www.facebook.com/whiskeyatartemis/" target="_blank">Facebook ↗</a> <a class="di-link" href="https://www.yelp.ca/biz/artemis-whiskey-bar-victoria" target="_blank">Yelp ↗</a>
