        <div class="tip-box"><div class="tip-txt">Budapest has 7 Michelin-starred restaurants as of the 2026 Guide (verified July 2026): two-star Stand, plus one-star Babel, Borkonyha, Costes, Essência, Rumour, and Salt. Since Al Habtoor and Kempinski are literally next door to each other on Erzsébet tér, distances below apply to <strong>both hotels equally</strong>. Book 3-4 weeks ahead minimum for Stand especially — it sells out.</div></div>

        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Stand ⭐⭐</div><div class="rc-type">Modern Hungarian · Székely Mihály u. 2 · ~10-12 min walk · ~89,500 HUF (~$250) 8-course</div><div class="rc-desc">Budapest's only two-star, run by two of Hungary's most famous chefs (Tamás Széll & Szabina Szulló). Called "the pinnacle of Hungarian fine dining" — an 8-course tasting menu that reinterprets Hungarian classics with serious technique. Wine pairing runs the price up to ~€400 total.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Books up to 60 days out and genuinely sells out — reserve the moment your dates are locked in. If you only do one splurge dinner in Budapest, make it this one.</div><div class="rc-tip">⭐ Consistently the top-rated of the group. <strong>Order:</strong> whatever's in the current tasting menu — there's no à la carte, and the surprise format is part of the experience.</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stand+Etterem+Szekely+Mihaly+utca+2+Budapest" target="_blank">View on map ↗</a><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g274887-d13116899-Reviews-Stand-Budapest_Central_Hungary.html" target="_blank">Reviews ↗</a></div>

        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Costes ⭐</div><div class="rc-type">Modern European · Ráday u. 4 · ~20-25 min walk or short taxi · ~€120-150 (~$130-165) tasting</div><div class="rc-desc">The trailblazer — Hungary's first-ever Michelin star, awarded 2010. A 7-course tasting menu built on French fine-dining technique with Hungarian ingredients woven in. Located in District IX, a bit outside the tourist core, but a genuine culinary landmark.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Some recent reviews suggest it's due for a refresh after 15+ years — still excellent, but Stand and Salt are getting more of the current buzz. Good pick if you want the "first and most storied" experience specifically.</div><div class="rc-tip"><strong>Order:</strong> the wine pairing — Costes has one of the more thoughtful lists in the city for showcasing Hungarian regions.</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Costes+Restaurant+Raday+utca+4+Budapest" target="_blank">View on map ↗</a><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g274887-d1994871-Reviews-Costes-Budapest_Central_Hungary.html" target="_blank">Reviews ↗</a></div>

        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Borkonyha Winekitchen ⭐</div><div class="rc-type">Modern Hungarian · Sas u. 3 · ~5 min walk (closest to your hotels) · ~€90-120 (~$100-130) tasting</div><div class="rc-desc">"Wine kitchen" by name and nature — around 200 wines on the list alongside bold, flavor-forward Hungarian cooking. One of the longest-holding stars in the city (a decade running) and the most tourist-accessible of the group, both in location and atmosphere.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 The single closest starred restaurant to Al Habtoor/Kempinski — genuinely walkable, no taxi needed. A great "easy" choice if you don't want to venture far after a travel day.</div><div class="rc-tip"><strong>Order:</strong> ask your server to build a wine flight around whatever Hungarian region interests you — this is the most wine-forward menu of the group.</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Borkonyha+Winekitchen+Sas+utca+3+Budapest" target="_blank">View on map ↗</a><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g274887-d1994868-Reviews-Borkonyha_Winekitchen-Budapest_Central_Hungary.html" target="_blank">Reviews ↗</a></div>

        <div class="rc"><div class="rc-name">Babel ⭐</div><div class="rc-type">Modern Hungarian/Transylvanian · Piarista köz 2 · ~10 min walk · €180 (~$195) 14-course — priciest of the group</div><div class="rc-desc">An elegant, hushed dining room with only a dozen tables, overlooking a Gothic cathedral near the Danube — genuinely one of the most romantic settings on this list. The 14-course tasting menu leans into Hungarian/Transylvanian roots with real technical precision. Rare local wine vintages on the list.</div><div class="rc-tip">💡 Best pick for a special-occasion, date-night feel over a food-nerd deep-dive — the room and pacing are built for a memorable evening, not just the plates.</div><div class="rc-tip"><strong>Order:</strong> the full wine pairing flight — sommelier János Gervai is himself a winemaker, and the pairing is built around major Hungarian wine regions specifically.</div><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Babel+Restaurant+Piarista+koz+2+Budapest" target="_blank">View on map ↗</a><a class="rc-lnk" href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g274887-d10352914-Reviews-Babel-Budapest_Central_Hungary.html" target="_blank">Reviews ↗</a></div>

