        <div style="padding:12px;background:var(--acb);border:2px solid var(--b);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:10px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);font-weight:500">One shore excursion per day included with your Vista Balcony Suite. Booking opens closer to departure. Your wishlist below:</div>
        <div id="dn-exc-list">
          <div class="exc-item"><div class="exc-hdr" onclick="toggleExc(this)"><div class="exc-bar"></div><div class="exc-main"><div class="exc-day">Day 2 · Budapest</div><div class="exc-name">Budapest Panoramic Walking & River Tour</div><div class="exc-meta">Buda Castle · Parliament · Chain Bridge · ~3-4 hrs guided, rest of day free</div></div><div class="exc-price">Included</div><div class="exc-chevron">▶</div></div><div class="exc-body"><div class="exc-desc">Budapest's two halves — hilly Buda and flat Pest — are connected by the iconic Chain Bridge. Buda Castle District and Fisherman's Bastion offer panoramic views. Don't miss the Central Market Hall for local food and wine tasting. Sunset from Gellért Hill over the Danube is extraordinary.</div></div></div>
          <div class="exc-item"><div class="exc-hdr" onclick="toggleExc(this)"><div class="exc-bar" style="background:#0891b2"></div><div class="exc-main"><div class="exc-day" style="color:#0891b2">Day 3 · Bratislava</div><div class="exc-name">Bratislava Old Town & Castle</div><div class="exc-meta">Slovakia's capital · Castle hill · UFO Tower · ~2.5-3 hrs guided, rest of day free</div></div><div class="exc-price">Included</div><div class="exc-chevron">▶</div></div><div class="exc-body"><div class="exc-desc">The smallest and most walkable of the trip's capital cities — Old Town is compact, cobblestoned, and dotted with quirky bronze statues (look for "Čumil," the grinning man peeking out of a manhole). Bratislava Castle sits on a hill directly above the river with sweeping views over the Danube and into Austria and Hungary on a clear day. St. Martin's Cathedral, where Hungarian kings were once crowned, and the UFO Observation Deck atop the SNP Bridge (a genuinely odd Soviet-era flying-saucer-shaped tower with a restaurant) round out the highlights. Since it's a smaller city, this tends to be a more relaxed, lower-key day than Budapest or Vienna.</div></div></div>
          <div class="exc-item"><div class="exc-hdr" onclick="toggleExc(this)"><div class="exc-bar" style="background:#7c3aed"></div><div class="exc-main"><div class="exc-day" style="color:#7c3aed">Days 4–5 · Vienna ✦ Overnight</div><div class="exc-name">Vienna Imperial Experience</div><div class="exc-meta">Schönbrunn · Ringstrasse · Naschmarkt · Opera · ~4 hrs guided/day, overnight for dinner</div></div><div class="exc-price">Included</div><div class="exc-chevron">▶</div></div><div class="exc-body"><div class="exc-desc">Schönbrunn Palace (Habsburg summer residence, 1,441 rooms) and its immaculate gardens. The Ringstrasse boulevard features the Opera House, Parliament, and Kunsthistorisches Museum in a single grand sweep. The Naschmarkt is 1.5 km of food stalls — your best daytime food experience in Vienna. The overnight stay gives you a real evening for your Steirereck or Mraz & Sohn dinner!</div></div></div>
          <div class="exc-item"><div class="exc-hdr" onclick="toggleExc(this)"><div class="exc-bar"></div><div class="exc-main"><div class="exc-day">Day 6 · Wachau Valley + Melk</div><div class="exc-name">Melk Abbey + Wachau Wine Tasting 🍷</div><div class="exc-meta">UNESCO monastery · Vineyard Heuriger · Dürnstein · ~3 hrs guided + optional wine tasting add-on</div></div><div class="exc-price">Included</div><div class="exc-chevron">▶</div></div><div class="exc-body"><div class="exc-desc">Melk Abbey is one of the most spectacular Baroque monasteries in Europe, dramatically perched above the Danube. Dürnstein village (where Richard the Lionheart was imprisoned!) has a ruined castle above it with extraordinary views — 30-min hike. Wine tastings at Heuriger (wine taverns) where you taste Grüner Veltliner and Riesling poured directly by the producers. Look for Smaragd-classified wines — the region's top designation.</div></div></div>
          <div class="exc-item"><div class="exc-hdr" onclick="toggleExc(this)"><div class="exc-bar" style="background:#b45309"></div><div class="exc-main"><div class="exc-day" style="color:#b45309">Day 7 · Engelhartszell, Austria</div><div class="exc-name">Stift Engelszell Monastery + Trappist Beer</div><div class="exc-meta">Austria's only Trappist monastery · Rococo church · ~2 hrs guided, relaxed day</div></div><div class="exc-price">Included</div><div class="exc-chevron">▶</div></div><div class="exc-body"><div class="exc-desc">A tiny riverside village whose main draw is Stift Engelszell — the only Trappist monastery in Austria, founded in 1293. The monks brew their own Trappist beer and liqueur on-site (one of only a handful of Trappist breweries in the world), and the abbey church is a beautifully over-the-top Rococo interior that feels surprising for such a small, quiet town. A gentle, slower-paced final port day before crossing into Germany at Vilshofen the next morning — good for a relaxed last taste of Austria and a beer tasting to close out the trip.</div></div></div>
        </div>
