        <div class="tip-box" style="border-color:#f59e0b;background:rgba(245,158,11,.08)"><div class="tip-lbl" style="color:#92400e">⏳ Don't transfer points yet</div><div class="tip-txt">Airlines only release schedules ~11 months out, so Aug 2027 flights won't be searchable until roughly <strong>September 2026</strong>. Chase/Amex transfers are one-way and can't be undone — wait until you can see real award availability before moving anything.</div></div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:10px">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">🌐 The Route</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.6">Cruise sails Budapest → Vilshofen, Germany (one-way). Fly into Budapest either way (fastest routing, one realistic stopover of ~1.5-2.5h = <strong>~12-12.5h total</strong>, e.g. via Frankfurt or Amsterdam — longer than the bare-minimum layover since you clear EU immigration at that first stop). Fly home from <strong>Munich</strong> (nearest hub to Vilshofen) if no extension, or from <strong>Prague</strong> if you do the After-Stay (fastest routing, one stopover of ~1.5-2h = <strong>~11.5-12h total</strong>, e.g. via Reykjavik). This is an open-jaw itinerary — you don't need one program to cover both legs; mix and match whatever prices/redeems best per leg.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:10px;border:2px solid #22c55e">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">🔵 United Miles — One of Three Pools, Not "Fly United"</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.6">United miles book any Star Alliance-operated flight, not just United-branded planes — reachable from <strong>both your existing United balance AND Chase transfers (1:1)</strong>, so Chase can top off whatever a specific date needs. No fuel surcharges on award tickets, and the search tool shows Star Alliance partner space directly (Lufthansa, Austrian, SWISS all serve this region well — Austrian flies direct to Vienna). <strong>Eric has United elite status</strong> too — worth checking his tier, since it can mean complimentary upgrades and priority treatment on Star Alliance partner flights, not just United metal. Strong option for IAD→BUD and PRG→IAD, but compare against the others below before committing.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:10px">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:6px">🟦 Chase Ultimate Rewards — Backup Options</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ts);line-height:1.6">Beyond United, Chase also reaches <strong>Air France/KLM Flying Blue</strong> (serves both Budapest and Prague via Paris/Amsterdam — watch for their "Promo Reward" flash pricing, sometimes well below standard rates) and <strong>British Airways/Iberia Avios</strong> (distance-based pricing, though BA-operated transatlantic legs carry high surcharges — Iberia metal doesn't).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hi" style="margin-bottom:10px">
